      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Since $AB$ is the diameter of the circle, $\\angle ABI =\\angle ECI=\\angle CBI=90^\\circ$.  Thus, $\\angle ABI=90^\\circ-\\angle ABI=\\angle CBI=90^\\circ-\\angle CBI$.\n\nWe will investigate the following inequalities for $\\angle ABI$: (i) $0^\\circ<\\angle ABI<90^\\circ$, (ii) $0^\\circ<\\angle ABI<65^\\circ$, and (iii) $0^\\circ<\\angle ABI<40^\\circ.$  We will investigate the following inequalities for $\\angle CBI$: (iv) $0^\\circ<\\angle CBI<90^\\circ$, (v) $0^\\circ<\\angle CBI<50^\\circ$, and (vi) $0^\\circ<\\angle CBI<20^\\circ$.\n\nWe have $\\angle ABI=\\angle CBI$.  So, $\\angle ABI<\\angle ABI$, which is a contradiction.  Therefore, $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ,$ $\\angle ABI<65^\\circ,$ and $\\angle ABI<40^\\circ.$\n\nSince $\\angle ABI<65^\\circ$, we have $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ,$ which leads to $\\angle ABI+\\angle ABI<120^\\circ$.  Thus, the $\\angle ABI+\\angle ABI<120^\\circ$ or $\\angle ABI+\\angle ABI<120^\\circ.$\n\nSince we already have $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ,$ we have $\\angle ABI+\\angle ABI<180^\\circ.$  Thus, the conclusion $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ$ and $\\angle ABI<40^\\circ$ is unsatisfiable.\n\nTherefore, we have $\\angle ABI>\\angle ABI$ and $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ,$ which implies $\\angle ABI+\\angle ABI<180^\\circ.$  Thus, the conclusion $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ$ and $\\angle ABI<40^\\circ$ is unsatisfiable.\n\nTherefore, $\\angle ABI>\\angle ABI$ and $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ,$ which implies $\\angle ABI+\\angle ABI<180^\\circ.$  Thus, the conclusion $\\angle ABI<90^\\circ$ and $\\angle ABI<40^\\circ$ is unsatisfiable. Therefore, we have $60^\\circ<\\angle ABI<90^\\circ$ or $0^\\circ<\\angle ABI<40^\\circ,$ but we know that we can eliminate the possibility of $60^\\circ<\\angle ABI<90^\\circ.$  Therefore, the only solution is $\\boxed{25^\\circ}.$. The answer is 25",
